{
  "id": "h3",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "title": "Notifications: cursors, soft deletes & async forEach",
  "minutes": 40,
  "tagline": "Infinite scroll shows duplicates, 'mark all read' half-works, deleted items still count, and anyone can delete anything.",
  "tags": ["cursor pagination", "async loops", "soft delete", "IDOR"],
  "lookFor": [
    "Cursor pagination: the next page starts strictly AFTER the cursor. `$lt`/`$gt`, never `$lte`/`$gte`.",
    "`array.forEach(async …)` does not wait for anything. Use `for…of` with await, or `Promise.all(map)`.",
    "Soft delete means EVERY read path must filter `deletedAt: null`: lists, counts, lookups.",
    "Every `/:id` mutation: does it check the record belongs to the caller?",
    "nextCursor must be null when there's nothing left, or clients loop forever on empty pages."
  ],
  "bugs": [
    {
      "symptom": "Page 2 repeats the last item of page 1",
      "file": "src/repositories/notificationRepo.js",
      "hints": [
        "nextCursor is the seq of the last item shown. Should page 2 include that seq?"
      ],
      "cause": "`seq: { $lte: cursor }` includes the cursor item itself, so each page boundary item shows up twice.",
      "fix": "`seq: { $lt: cursor }`",
      "pattern": "Inclusive cursor"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "Unread count includes deleted notifications",
      "file": "src/repositories/notificationRepo.js",
      "hints": [
        "Compare the filter in `list` with the filter in `countUnread`."
      ],
      "cause": "`countUnread` forgets `deletedAt: null`, so soft-deleted items still bump the badge.",
      "fix": "`items.count({ userId, read: false, deletedAt: null })`",
      "pattern": "Soft-delete filter missing on one read path"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "'Mark all read' leaves unread items",
      "file": "src/services/notificationService.js",
      "hints": [
        "What does `forEach` do with the Promise your async callback returns?"
      ],
      "cause": "`unread.forEach(async (n) => await repo.markRead(n._id))` fires the writes and returns immediately. The response goes out (and the next request reads) before they finish.",
      "fix": "`await Promise.all(unread.map((n) => repo.markRead(n._id)));` (or a single updateMany)",
      "pattern": "async forEach"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "nextCursor is set on the last page",
      "file": "src/services/notificationService.js",
      "hints": [
        "How do you know there's another page if you only fetched `limit` rows?"
      ],
      "cause": "`nextCursor` is always the last item's seq, even when nothing is left, so clients request one more empty page forever.",
      "fix": "Fetch `limit + 1` rows; `hasMore = rows.length > limit`; return `rows.slice(0, limit)` and `nextCursor = hasMore ? last.seq : null`.",
      "pattern": "Missing 'has more' check"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "(hidden) Users can delete other users' notifications",
      "file": "src/services/notificationService.js",
      "hints": [
        "remove(userId, id): is userId used at all?"
      ],
      "cause": "`remove` soft-deletes by id without checking `n.userId === userId`. That's an IDOR.",
      "fix": "`if (!n || n.userId !== userId || n.deletedAt !== null) throw new NotFoundError(...)`",
      "pattern": "Missing ownership check (IDOR)"
    }
  ]
}
@@@ ticket.md
# NOTIF-88: Notification centre bugs

The mobile team reports: **infinite scroll shows duplicates**, the **red badge never clears** after "mark all as read", and **deleted notifications still count**. Also a pen-test finding about deleting other users' data.

## API (header `x-user-id`)
| Method | Path | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/notifications?limit=&cursor=` | Newest first. `{ items, nextCursor }`. `nextCursor` = `null` when no more pages. Pages never overlap. Deleted items are never shown. |
| `GET` | `/notifications/unread-count` | `{ count }`, excluding deleted |
| `POST` | `/notifications/read-all` | Marks all of the caller's notifications read before responding. `{ updated }` |
| `DELETE` | `/notifications/:id` | Soft delete, **204**. Not yours / unknown / already deleted → **404** |

Tests create notifications with `notificationService.notify(userId, text)`. Each gets an increasing `seq`.
